  "version": 2,
  "note": "The families dataset, version 2: sixteen scripted sessions across the eight layout families of layout version 3, the four visual presets, five viewport sizes and three content lengths, and the stress-test set. It replaces version 1, whose layout had no grouping and no alignment of its own. It exists to show that the generator varies structure and not only appearance, that every validator passes what it writes, and that the validators reject each stress test for the reason it states. It is small enough for the command-line test to generate in seconds, and it is not the pilot. A design is dealt whole: a layout family, a visual preset and a content length, then the least used viewport size in which every state of the session passes the validators. A changed dataset is a new version of this file, never an edit to this one.",
